<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Federal Electoral Institute</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1990">1990</a>–<a href="/years/2014">2014</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Instituto Federal Electoral</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Federal Electoral Institute (IFE) was the body that organised federal elections in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> from 1990 to 2014. Created after the disputed election of 1988 and made independent of the government in 1996, it introduced photo voter cards and impartial administration that made possible the opposition victory of 2000. It was replaced by the National Electoral Institute in 2014.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/federal-electoral-institute.jpg" alt="Federal Electoral Institute" width="320" height="291" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Omar Alejandro Covarrubias Neri based on the arms by Francisco Eppens Helguera (1968) and Juan Manuel Gabino Villascán. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Mexico.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
